{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   Implement 10 SOS (Strixhaven-themed) Magic: The Gathering card implementations in `/workspace/cards/sos/`, collector numbers: **1, 4, 13, 57, 97, 120, 201, 226, 245, 257**. Each card directory has `card_spec.json` (metadata) and `card_impl.py` (stub to fill). The user explicitly said:\n   - Use completed FDN cards in `/workspace/cards/fdn/` as implementation examples.\n   - Refer to `RULEBOOK.txt` for full rules (grep, don't read whole — 961KB).\n   - Read engine source modules directly for API (rich docstrings): `engine/card.py`, `engine/events.py`, `engine/triggers.py`, `engine/replacement_effects.py`, `engine/zones.py`.\n   - \"You are expected to make changes to the engine to implement new keywords and mechanics. The existing code base may not be perfect, you are free to make changes that don't break current behavior.\"\n\n   **CRITICAL CONSTRAINTS (must persist verbatim):**\n   - User: \"Do not modify any files under workspace/engine_tests/. These tests are staged for your local verification only; the runner uses its own authoritative copies for grading. Modifying the workspace tests will not change your score — it will only mislead you about whether your engine changes are correct.\"\n   - AGENTS.md Hard Rules: (1) Each card's implementation class must remain in `cards/sos/{card_id}/card_impl.py`; do not move/rename card directories. (2) Treat `engine_tests/` as read-only (no modify/add/delete); do NOT modify/delete existing FDN reference tests at `cards/fdn/fdn_*/tests.py` (may read, never edit); own SOS tests belong at `cards/sos/sos_<N>/tests.py`. (3) Additive-only engine modifications: MAY add new methods/classes/helpers/files inside `engine/` and MAY modify bodies of existing functions, but MUST NOT rename, move, or delete anything that already exists in `engine/` (no refactoring — breaks grader imports and zeros the score).\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - MTG engine (Python): zones, LIFO stack, triggers (APNAP), replacement effects (\"instead\" semantics), continuous effects (7-layer system), state-based actions, combat.\n   - Card hierarchy: GameObject → CardImpl → Creature/Instant/Sorcery/Enchantment/Aura/Artifact/ArtifactCreature/Planeswalker/Land.\n   - CardImpl hooks: `can_cast`, `cost_reduction(game)->int`, `on_cast`, `on_resolve`, `get_targets(game)->list[TargetRequirement]`, `register_triggers`, `register_replacement_effects`, `get_activated_abilities`, `get_modes`. Planeswalker: `get_loyalty_abilities()->list[LoyaltyAbility]`. Land: `get_mana_abilities()->list[ManaAbility]`, `can_cast`→False.\n   - Mechanics to build: Converge, Counterspell, Planeswalker loyalty, Affinity, cost-reduction-per-graveyard-card, attacks trigger, free-cast from graveyard/exile, Surveil, Miracle, Casualty, Paradigm, Prepared (split-card), keywords (Reach/Flying/Vigilance/Deathtouch/Haste), coin flips + skip turns, land-becomes-creature, delayed \"beginning of main phase\" triggers.\n   - `ManaCost.parse(\"{1}{U}{U}\")`; `ManaCost.cmc = generic + sum(pips.values()) + len(hybrid)` (X treated as 0); `cast_spell` sets `card.colors_spent = list(player.mana_pool.last_payment_colors)`.\n   - DeterministicPlayer pops one scripted answer per choose/choose_target/choose_yes_no/choose_card/assign_damage_order call.\n   - test_utils.cast_spell resolves the ENTIRE stack and RAISES if `game.stack` is not empty (even for instants) — so counterspell tests must use `engine.casting.cast_spell` directly + manual resolution.\n   - priority_loop's `_get_legal_actions` returns [] always — players cannot cast via priority; tests drive casting via cast_spell/activate_ability and resolve via resolve_top / popping stack.\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - `/workspace/AGENTS.md`, `/workspace/PROJECT_MAP.md` — orientation + hard rules. FDN cards with tests.py: fdn_13, fdn_142, fdn_205, fdn_215, fdn_244. Bare imports (workspace root on sys.path).\n   - `/workspace/engine/card.py` — `Creature` has base_power/base_toughness, modified_power/modified_toughness, plus_one_counters/minus_one_counters, `_reset_characteristics()` (resets card_types→original, keywords, and for Creature P/T to base), properties `power`/`toughness`. `Land` has no P/T. Dataclasses: `LoyaltyAbility(loyalty_cost, effect, description)`, `ManaAbility(cost, mana_produced, description)`.\n   - `/workspace/engine/casting.py` — `get_cost_reduction(game, card, controller)` queries `card.cost_reduction(game)`, clamps to generic. `cast_spell` pays, then `card.colors_spent = list(...)`. `cast_spell_free(game, player, card, from_zone)` casts without paying. `_resolve_spell` sets `card.chosen_targets = stack_obj.targets`, calls on_resolve, then move_to_zone (permanents→battlefield, instants/sorceries→graveyard).\n   - `/workspace/engine/events.py` — **MODIFIED** (Edit #1): added `BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent(TriggeredEvent)` with fields `phase: Any = None`, `player: Any = None`. Existing: SpellCastTriggeredEvent(spell, player, card, controller), AttacksTriggeredEvent(creature, attacker), MoveToGraveyardReplacementEvent (destination/prevented/card), CreatureDiesReplacementEvent, etc.\n   - `/workspace/engine/turn.py` — **MODIFIED** (Edit #2): run_turn now fires BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent at main phases:\n     ```python\n     elif game.phase in (Phase.PRECOMBAT_MAIN, Phase.POSTCOMBAT_MAIN) and game.step is None:\n         from engine.events import BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent\n         game.trigger_manager.fire_event(game, BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent(phase=game.phase, player=game.active_player))\n     ```\n   - `/workspace/engine/combat.py` — `declare_attackers_step` sets is_attacking, taps unless vigilance; does NOT yet fire AttacksTriggeredEvent (planned edit).