{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   Implement 10 SOS (Strixhaven-themed) Magic: The Gathering card implementations in `/workspace/cards/sos/`, collector numbers: **1, 4, 13, 57, 97, 120, 201, 226, 245, 257**. Each card directory has `card_spec.json` (metadata) and `card_impl.py` (stub to fill with the implementation class). User instructions:\n   - Use completed FDN cards in `/workspace/cards/fdn/` as implementation examples.\n   - Refer to `RULEBOOK.txt` for full rules (grep, don't read whole — ~961KB).\n   - Read engine source modules directly for API (rich docstrings).\n   - \"You are expected to make changes to the engine to implement new keywords and mechanics. The existing code base may not be perfect, you are free to make changes that don't break current behavior.\"\n\n   **CRITICAL CONSTRAINTS (must persist verbatim):**\n   - User: \"Do not modify any files under workspace/engine_tests/. These tests are staged for your local verification only; the runner uses its own authoritative copies for grading. Modifying the workspace tests will not change your score — it will only mislead you about whether your engine changes are correct.\"\n   - AGENTS.md Hard Rules: (1) Each card's implementation class must remain in `cards/sos/{card_id}/card_impl.py`; do not move/rename card directories. (2) Treat `engine_tests/` as read-only (no modify/add/delete); do NOT modify/delete existing FDN reference tests at `cards/fdn/fdn_*/tests.py` (may read, never edit); own SOS tests belong at `cards/sos/sos_<N>/tests.py`. (3) Additive-only engine modifications: MAY add new methods/classes/helpers/files inside `engine/` and MAY modify bodies of existing functions, but MUST NOT rename, move, or delete anything that already exists in `engine/` (no refactoring — breaks grader imports and zeros the score).\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - MTG engine (Python): zones, LIFO stack, triggers (APNAP), replacement effects, continuous effects (7-layer system), state-based actions, combat.\n   - Card hierarchy: GameObject → CardImpl → Creature/Instant/Sorcery/Enchantment/Aura/Artifact/ArtifactCreature/Planeswalker/Land.\n   - CardImpl hooks: `can_cast(game)->bool`, `cost_reduction(game)->int`, `on_cast(game)`, `on_resolve(game)`, `get_targets(game)->list[TargetRequirement]`, `register_triggers(game)`, `register_replacement_effects(game)`, `get_activated_abilities()->list[ActivatedAbility]`, `get_modes()`. Planeswalker: `get_loyalty_abilities()->list[LoyaltyAbility]`. Land: `get_mana_abilities()->list[ManaAbility]`, `can_cast`→False.\n   - **Two ContinuousEffect classes**: the real one is `engine.continuous_effects.ContinuousEffect(source, layer, sublayer=None, apply=callable(game), timestamp=0, duration=DURATION_PERMANENT)`. The card.py one (apply/remove/description) is legacy — DO NOT use it. Layer enum: COPY=1,CONTROL=2,TEXT=3,TYPE=4,COLOR=5,ABILITY=6,POWER_TOUGHNESS=7. SubLayer: CHARACTERISTIC_DEFINING=\"7a\", SET_PT=\"7b\", MODIFY_PT=\"7c\", COUNTERS=\"7d\". DURATION_PERMANENT=-1, DURATION_END_OF_TURN=0. `game.effect_manager.add(effect)`. apply_all resets battlefield objects via `_reset_characteristics()` then applies effects in layer/timestamp order. CardImpl._reset_characteristics resets only card_types (to _original) and keywords; Creature subclass additionally resets modified_power/toughness and counters. Land is NOT a Creature so reset does NOT touch its P/T attributes.\n   - `TriggerRegistration(event_type, condition, effect, source, controller)`. `condition(game, event)->bool` receives the event object. `effect(game)` receives ONLY game (no event). `fire_event(game, event)` matches by isinstance (subclasses match), checks condition once per trigger, pushes StackObjects in APNAP order. `game.trigger_manager.register(reg)`, `.unregister(source)` (identity-based).\n   - Loyalty/activated abilities: card.py dataclasses `LoyaltyAbility(loyalty_cost, effect, description)`, `ActivatedAbility(cost, effect, description)`, `ManaAbility(cost, mana_produced, description)`. Runtime: `engine.abilities.LoyaltyAbilityInstance(source, controller, loyalty_cost, effect, description)` and `ActivatedAbilityInstance(source, controller, cost, effect, is_mana_ability, description)`. `activate_ability(game, player, instance)` drives them. Loyalty: sorcery-speed, once-per-turn, adjusts source.loyalty, pushes StackObject. Ajani's loyalty effects read `getattr(pw, \"_resolve_target\", None)` (set by driver/test before resolution). `tap_cost(game, source)->bool`.\n   - `cast_spell` sets `card.colors_spent = list(mana_pool.last_payment_colors)` (a LIST) and now `card.mana_spent = mana_pool.last_payment_total`. Converge cards must handle colors_spent as both int (tests) and list (real cast).\n   - `cast_spell_free(game, player, card, from_zone)` casts without paying; now sets `card.mana_spent = 0` and fires SpellCastTriggeredEvent.\n   - `_resolve_spell`: sets `card.chosen_targets`, calls on_resolve, then moves permanents→battlefield, else (NEW) if `card._exile_instead_of_graveyard` → exile (resets flag), else → graveyard. Does NOT pass replacement_event for instant/sorcery resolution.\n   - move_to_zone: fires ETB BEFORE register_triggers (so self-ETB triggers go in on_resolve like Wardens); only unregisters triggers/replacements when leaving battlefield. move_zone clears colors_spent.\n   - DeterministicPlayer: choose/choose_target/choose_yes_no/choose_card/assign_damage_order each pop one scripted answer (`_pop`); raises ScriptExhaustedError when empty; `player._script.appendleft(x)` injects answers.\n   - test_utils: `cast_spell(game, idx, name, targets=)` scripts targets via `player._script.appendleft(reversed(targets))`, resolves ENTIRE stack via `_resolve_top_of_stack` (errors if stack still has items it can't resolve). `declare_attackers(game, [names])` scripts attacker list, calls declare_attackers_step, NO priority_loop after. `set_board_state(game, idx, *, battlefield, hand, graveyard, life, mana)`. `create_game(deck1, deck2, *, scripts=(s1,s2), player1_life, player2_life)`.\n   - Counterspell helper pattern (from fdn_48 Refute): `_get_chosen_target(card,game)` reads chosen_targets[0] or `_resolve_target`; `_counter_spell(game, stack_obj)` removes from `game.stack._items`, removes card from controller's STACK zone, adds to owner's GRAVEYARD. `can_cast` True only if non-self spell on stack; `get_targets` returns `[TargetRequirement(filter_fn=lambda obj: obj is not self and getattr(obj,\"is_spell\",True), description=\"target spell\", zone=Zone.STACK)]`.\n   - `engine.game` helpers: `deal_damage`, `destroy`, `sacrifice(game,player,perm)`, `exile`, `draw_card(game,player)` (increments player.cards_drawn_this_turn then fires DrawsCardTriggeredEvent), `discard(game,player,card)`, `create_token(game,player,token)`, `add_counter`, `remove_counter`, `tap`, `untap`.\n   - `copy_spell(game, original_stackobj, controller, new_targets=None)` (engine.stack) shallow-copies source, binds on_resolve to copied_card.on_resolve (no zone move).\n   - ManaCost.parse(\"{1}{U}{U}\"); `ManaCost(generic=5)`; `cmc = generic + sum(pips.values()) + len(hybrid)`. Keyword enum has NO AFFINITY/PREPARED/PARADIGM/MIRACLE/SURVEIL/CONVERGE/CASUALTY — only evergreen (FLYING, FIRST_STRIKE, DOUBLE_STRIKE, DEATHTOUCH, TRAMPLE, LIFELINK, VIGILANCE, REACH, HASTE, FLASH, DEFENDER, HEXPROOF, INDESTRUCTIBLE, MENACE, WARD, PROWESS). So set only real keyword flags (e.g. Witherbloom = FLYING|DEATHTOUCH; Silverquill = FLYING|VIGILANCE; Lorehold = FLYING|HASTE; Dawning Archaic = REACH).\n   - Surveil simplified (fdn_49): take top of library, optionally move to graveyard.\n   - Land mana abilities (fdn_267): ManaAbility(cost=_tap_cost, mana_produced=_effect adds to source.controller.mana_pool, description). Color restrictions NOT enforced (engine limitation).\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - `/workspace/engine/events.py` — (prior session) added `BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent(TriggeredEvent)` with fields `phase: Any = None`, `player: Any = None` (after BeginningOfCombatTriggeredEvent). Existing events confirmed: SpellCastTriggeredEvent(spell, player, card, controller), AttacksTriggeredEvent(creature, attacker), DrawsCardTriggeredEvent(player, card), BeginningOfUpkeepTriggeredEvent (NO player field), CreatureDiesTriggeredEvent, MoveToGraveyardReplacementEvent (destination/prevented/card), etc.\n   - `/workspace/engine/turn.py` — (prior session) run_turn fires BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent at main phases (lines 207-214):\n     ```python\n     elif game.phase in (Phase.PRECOMBAT_MAIN, Phase.POSTCOMBAT_MAIN) and game.step is None:\n         from engine.events import BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent\n         game.trigger_manager.fire_event(game, BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent(phase=game.phase, player=game.active_player))\n     ```\n   - `/workspace/engine/combat.py` — **EDITED THIS SESSION**: declare_attackers_step now collects `declared: list[Any]` and after the attacker loop fires:\n     ```python\n     if declared:\n         from engine.events import AttacksTriggeredEvent\n         for attacker in declared:\n             game.trigger_manager.fire_event(game, AttacksTriggeredEvent(creature=attacker, attacker=attacker))\n     ```\n   - `/workspace/engine/mana.py` — **EDITED THIS SESSION**: added `self._last_payment_total: int = 0` in __init__; added property `last_payment_total` returning `self._last_payment_total`; in `pay()` after computing colors: `self._last_payment_total = sum(self._pool.values()) - sum(working.values())` (before `self._pool = working`).\n   - `/workspace/engine/casting.py` — **EDITED THIS SESSION (4 edits)**:\n     (a) In cast_spell after payment: `card.mana_spent = player.mana_pool.last_payment_total` and after push: `_fire_spell_cast(game, card, player)`.\n     (b) In cast_spell_free before on_cast: `card.mana_spent = 0`; after push: `_fire_spell_cast(game, card, player)`; added helper:\n     ```python\n     def _fire_spell_cast(game, card, player):\n         from engine.events import SpellCastTriggeredEvent\n         game.trigger_manager.fire_event(game, SpellCastTriggeredEvent(spell=card, player=player, card=card, controller=player))\n     ```\n     (c) get_cost_reduction now: `raw += _external_cost_reduction(game, card, controller)` before clamp; added helper:\n     ```python\n     def _external_cost_reduction(game, card, controller):\n         total = 0\n         for perm in game.get_battlefield(controller).get_all():\n             if perm is card: continue\n             hook = getattr(perm, \"static_cost_reduction\", None)\n             if hook is None: continue\n             amount = hook(game, card, controller)\n             if amount: total += amount\n         return total\n     ```\n     (d) _resolve_spell non-permanent branch now: `elif getattr(card, \"_exile_instead_of_graveyard\", False): card._exile_instead_of_graveyard = False; move_to_zone(game, card, Zone.STACK, Zone.EXILE)` else graveyard.\n   - `/workspace/engine/game_state.py` — **EDITED THIS SESSION**: added `self.skip_turns: dict[int, int] = {0: 0, 1: 0}` in __init__; in advance_phase end-of-turn normal branch added:\n     ```python\n     elif self.skip_turns.get(self._normal_next_index, 0) > 0:\n         self.skip_turns[self._normal_next_index] -= 1\n         self.active_player_index = 1 - self._normal_next_index\n     ```\n     (between the extra_turns branch and the else that sets active_player_index = _normal_next_index). Traced correct: skip[1]=1 → A,A,B,A,B...; skip[1]=2 → A,A,A,B...\n   - Reference cards read (DO NOT MODIFY): fdn_48 (Refute counterspell), fdn_205 (Wardens converge + tests.py), fdn_134 (Ajani planeswalker loyalty), fdn_6 (Claws Out affinity/ContinuousEffect at Layer.POWER_TOUGHNESS/SubLayer.MODIFY_PT/DURATION_END_OF_TURN), fdn_92 (Rite of Dragoncaller SpellCastTriggeredEvent self-guarded with _is_on_battlefield), fdn_49 (surveil), fdn_267 (Secluded Courtyard land mana abilities), fdn_254 (Heraldic Banner mana abilities).\n   - All 10 SOS card_impl.py remain identical stubs (classes: TheDawningArchaic, TogetherAsOne, EmeritusOfTruceSwordsToPlowshares, ManaSculpt, RalZarekGuestLecturer, ImprovisationCapstone, LoreholdTheHistorian, SilverquillTheDisputant, WitherbloomTheBalancer, GreatHallOfTheBiblioplex).\n   - SOS specs confirmed this session: SOS 1 Dawning Archaic ({10} 7/7 Avatar Legendary, Reach, {1} less per inst/sorc in GY, attacks→may free-cast target inst/sorc from GY, exile-instead-of-GY). SOS 4 Together as One ({6} Sorcery Converge: target player draws X, deals X to any target, you gain X life, X=colors spent). SOS 13 Emeritus//Swords ({1}{W}{W} 3/3 Cat Cleric, Prepared; ETB target player creates 1/1 W/B Inkling flier, then if opp controls more creatures than you→prepared). SOS 57 Mana Sculpt ({1}{U}{U} Instant; counter target spell; if you control Wizard, add {C}=mana spent on it at beginning of your next main phase). SOS 97 Ral Zarek ({1}{B}{B} PW loyalty 3, Ral; +1 Surveil 2; -1 any number target players each discard; -2 return creature MV≤3 from your GY to bf; -7 flip 5 coins, target opp skips next X turns=heads). SOS 120 Improvisation Capstone ({5}{R}{R} Sorcery Lesson; exile top until total MV≥4, may cast any free; Paradigm). SOS 201 Lorehold ({3}{R}{W} 5/5 Elder Dragon flying haste; inst/sorc in hand have miracle {2}; at each opp upkeep may discard then draw). SOS 226 Silverquill ({2}{W}{B} 4/4 Elder Dragon flying vigilance; your inst/sorc spells have casualty 1). SOS 245 Witherbloom ({6}{B}{G} 5/5 Elder Dragon affinity for creatures, flying deathtouch; your inst/sorc spells have affinity for creatures). SOS 257 Great Hall ({T}:{C}; {T},pay 1 life: any color for inst/sorc only; {5}: if not a creature becomes 2/4 Wizard with \"whenever