{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   Implement 10 SOS (Strixhaven-themed) Magic: The Gathering card implementations in `/workspace/cards/sos/`, collector numbers: **1, 4, 13, 57, 97, 120, 201, 226, 245, 257**. Each card directory has `card_spec.json` (metadata) and `card_impl.py` (stub to fill with implementation class). User instructions:\n   - Use completed FDN cards in `/workspace/cards/fdn/` as implementation examples.\n   - Refer to `RULEBOOK.txt` for full rules (grep, don't read whole — ~961KB).\n   - Read engine source modules directly for API (rich docstrings).\n   - \"You are expected to make changes to the engine to implement new keywords and mechanics. The existing code base may not be perfect, you are free to make changes that don't break current behavior.\"\n\n   **CRITICAL CONSTRAINTS (must persist verbatim):**\n   - User: \"Do not modify any files under workspace/engine_tests/. These tests are staged for your local verification only; the runner uses its own authoritative copies for grading. Modifying the workspace tests will not change your score — it will only mislead you about whether your engine changes are correct.\"\n   - AGENTS.md Hard Rules: (1) Each card's implementation class must remain in `cards/sos/{card_id}/card_impl.py`; do not move/rename card directories. (2) Treat `engine_tests/` as read-only (no modify/add/delete); do NOT modify/delete existing FDN reference tests at `cards/fdn/fdn_*/tests.py` (may read, never edit); own SOS tests belong at `cards/sos/sos_<N>/tests.py`. (3) Additive-only engine modifications: MAY add new methods/classes/helpers/files inside `engine/` and MAY modify bodies of existing functions, but MUST NOT rename, move, or delete anything that already exists in `engine/` (no refactoring — breaks grader imports and zeros the score).\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - MTG engine (Python 3.11; use `python3`): zones, LIFO stack, triggers (APNAP), replacement effects, 7-layer continuous effects, state-based actions, combat.\n   - Card hierarchy (engine/card.py): GameObject → CardImpl → Creature/Instant/Sorcery/Enchantment/Aura/Artifact/ArtifactCreature/Planeswalker/Land. `subtypes: set[str]`; `supertypes: set[Supertype]`; `keywords: Keyword` (Flag). Creature has `base_power/base_toughness`, `modified_power/modified_toughness`, and `power`/`toughness` PROPERTIES (`modified + plus_one_counters - minus_one_counters`). Land.can_cast→False, has get_mana_abilities. Planeswalker has starting_loyalty/loyalty + get_loyalty_abilities.\n   - CardImpl hooks: `can_cast(game)->bool`, `cost_reduction(game)->int`, `on_cast(game)`, `on_resolve(game)`, `get_targets(game)->list[TargetRequirement]`, `register_triggers(game)`, `register_replacement_effects(game)`, `get_activated_abilities()->list[ActivatedAbility]`, `get_modes()`. NEW additive hook: `static_cost_reduction(game, spell, spell_controller)->int` (lets a permanent reduce OTHER spells' generic cost; summed in `_external_cost_reduction`).\n   - `TriggerRegistration(event_type, condition, effect, source, controller)`. `condition(game, event)->bool`; `effect(game)->None` (NO event). `fire_event(game, event)` matches by isinstance, evaluates condition once per trigger, pushes StackObjects APNAP. `game.trigger_manager.register/unregister(source)` (identity-based).\n   - Two ContinuousEffect classes: REAL one is `engine.continuous_effects.ContinuousEffect(source, layer, sublayer=None, apply=callable(game), timestamp=0, duration=DURATION_PERMANENT)`. Layer: COPY=1,CONTROL=2,TEXT=3,TYPE=4,COLOR=5,ABILITY=6,POWER_TOUGHNESS=7. SubLayer: CHARACTERISTIC_DEFINING=\"7a\", SET_PT=\"7b\", MODIFY_PT=\"7c\", COUNTERS=\"7d\". DURATION_PERMANENT=-1, DURATION_END_OF_TURN=0. `game.effect_manager.add(effect)`. apply_all resets battlefield via `_reset_characteristics()` then applies in layer/timestamp order. The card.py ContinuousEffect (apply/remove/description) is legacy — DO NOT use.\n   - Keyword enum (engine/types.py) has ONLY evergreen keywords: FLYING, FIRST_STRIKE, DOUBLE_STRIKE, DEATHTOUCH, TRAMPLE, LIFELINK, VIGILANCE, REACH, HASTE, FLASH, DEFENDER, HEXPROOF, INDESTRUCTIBLE, MENACE, WARD, PROWESS. NO Affinity/Casualty/Converge/Miracle/etc. Set only real flags.\n   - ManaType: WHITE/BLUE/BLACK/RED/GREEN/COLORLESS (`.value` = \"W\"/\"U\"/\"B\"/\"R\"/\"G\"/\"C\"). {C}=COLORLESS. ManaCost.parse(\"{1}{U}{U}\"); ManaCost(generic=N); `.cmc = generic + sum(pips.values()) + len(hybrid)`.\n   - Supertype: BASIC, LEGENDARY, SNOW.\n   - `cast_spell` sets `card.colors_spent = list(mana_pool.last_payment_colors)` (LIST) and `card.mana_spent = mana_pool.last_payment_total`; fires SpellCastTriggeredEvent. `cast_spell_free(game, player, card, from_zone)` sets `card.mana_spent = 0`, fires SpellCastTriggeredEvent, no payment/timing.\n   - `_resolve_spell`: sets card.chosen_targets, calls on_resolve, then permanents→battlefield, elif `_exile_instead_of_graveyard`→exile (resets flag), else→graveyard.\n   - `copy_spell(game, original_stackobj, controller, new_targets=None)`: shallow-copies source, binds on_resolve to copied_card.on_resolve, sets copied_card.chosen_targets; does NOT fire SpellCastTriggeredEvent (prevents casualty/cast-trigger loops); does NOT move zones.\n   - StackObject(source, controller, targets=[], on_resolve, is_mana_ability=False); `is_spell` not defined → counterspell filters use `getattr(obj,\"is_spell\",True)`.\n   - DeterministicPlayer._script is a deque: `append()` adds right, `popleft()` removes left; choose/choose_target/choose_yes_no/choose_card/assign_damage_order each pop one (raise ScriptExhaustedError when empty). test_utils.cast_spell scripts targets via `player._script.appendleft(target)` for `reversed(targets)`.\n   - test_utils: `cast_spell(game, idx, name, targets=)` resolves ENTIRE stack (auto-resolve) — UNSUITABLE for counterspell-on-stack setups; for those use `engine.casting.cast_spell` directly. `set_board_state(game, idx, *, battlefield, hand, graveyard, life, mana)` does NOT call register_triggers (must call manually in tests). `declare_attackers(game, [names])` does NOT priority_loop after.\n   - TESTING RULE: do NOT use priority_loop when scripted choices are pending (it consumes choose for \"pass\"). Resolve manually: `while not game.stack.is_empty(): game.stack.pop().on_resolve(game); resolve_state_based_actions(game)`.\n   - `engine.game` helpers: deal_damage(game,source,target,amount), destroy, sacrifice(game,player,perm), exile(game,obj), draw_card(game,player) (returns card; increments cards_drawn_this_turn; fires DrawsCardTriggeredEvent), discard(game,player,card), create_token(game,player,token), add_counter, remove_counter, tap, untap.\n   - `engine.casting.get_cost_reduction(game, card, controller)->int` is exported, clamps to generic, adds self cost_reduction + external; usable in unit tests.\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - `/workspace/engine/casting.py` — VERIFIED all prior edits in place: `card.mana_spent = player.mana_pool.last_payment_total` (line ~257) and `_fire_spell_cast(game, card, player)` (line 278) in cast_spell; `card.mana_spent = 0` (line 389) + `_fire_spell_cast` (line 409) in cast_spell_free; `_fire_spell_cast` helper (lines 416-429); `_external_cost_reduction` helper (lines 115-133, iterates controller battlefield calling `static_cost_reduction(game, card, controller)`); get_cost_reduction calls `raw += _external_cost_reduction(...)` (line 110); _resolve_spell exile branch (lines 466-470: `elif getattr(card, \"_exile_instead_of_graveyard\", False): card._exile_instead_of_graveyard = False; move_to_zone(game, card, Zone.STACK, Zone.EXILE)`).\n   - `/workspace/engine/combat.py` — declare_attackers_step fires (line 269) `AttacksTriggeredEvent(creature=attacker, attacker=attacker)` for each declared attacker.\n   - `/workspace/engine/events.py` — AttacksTriggeredEvent has fields `creature: Any=None`, `attacker: Any=None` (lines 119-121). BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent(phase, player) exists. SpellCastTriggeredEvent(spell, player, card, controller). DrawsCardTriggeredEvent(player, card). BeginningOfUpkeepTriggeredEvent (NO player field).\n   - `/workspace/engine/game_state.py` — has `skip_turns: dict[int,int] = {0:0,1:0}`; advance_phase consumes skip_turns in end-of-turn normal branch.\n   - `/workspace/engine/mana.py` — has `last_payment_total` property and `_last_payment_total` set in pay().\n   - `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_57/card_impl.py` (Mana Sculpt — DONE): Instant {1}{U}{U}. Helpers `_get_chosen_target`, `_counter_spell` (copied from Refute), `_controls_wizard`. `can_cast`/`get_targets` (target spell on stack). `on_resolve`: capture `mana_spent = getattr(getattr(target,\"source\",None),\"mana_spent\",0) or 0`, `_counter_spell`, then if controls Wizard call `_register_delayed_mana`. `_register_delayed_mana` registers one-shot TriggerRegistration on BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent (condition: `not state[\"done\"] and getattr(event,\"player\",None) is controller`; effect: set done, `controller.mana_pool.add(ManaType.COLORLESS, amount)`, `g.trigger_manager.unregister(self)`).\n   - `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_4/card_impl.py` (Together as One — DONE): Sorcery {6}, `self.colors_spent=0` in init. `_is_any_target(obj)` (creature or hasattr life). get_targets returns 2 TargetRequirements [player (hasattr life), any target]. `_converge_count()` returns len if list/set/tuple else int(cs). on_resolve: x=converge; if x<=0 return; chosen=chosen_targets; target_player draws X, damage_target takes X (deal_damage), controller.life += X.\n   - `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_226/card_impl.py` (Silverquill — DONE): Creature {2}{W}{B} 4/4 {\"Elder\",\"Dragon\"} LEGENDARY FLYING|VIGILANCE. `self._casualty_pending=[]`. Helpers `_is_on_battlefield`, `_is_instant_or_sorcery`. register_triggers on SpellCastTriggeredEvent: condition checks on-battlefield + spell is controller's inst/sorc + not self, then `source._casualty_pending.append(spell); return True` (append ONLY before True). effect calls `_resolve_casualty`: pop pending spell, find power>=1 creatures, choose_yes_no, choose_card, sacrifice, then find spell's StackObject and push copy_spell.\n   - `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_245/card_impl.py` (Witherbloom — DONE): Creature {6}{B}{G} 5/5 {\"Elder\",\"Dragon\"} LEGENDARY FLYING|DEATHTOUCH. Helpers `_is_on_battlefield`, `_is_instant_or_sorcery`, `_count_creatures`. `cost_reduction(game)` = count creatures controller controls. `static_cost_reduction(game, spell, spell_controller)` = if self on battlefield AND spell_controller is self.controller AND spell is inst/sorc → count_creatures(spell_controller) else 0.\n   - All 5 above have matching `tests.py` files; all pass (6+6+5+7 = and Mana Sculpt 6).\n   - Reference cards read: fdn_48 (Refute: _get_chosen_target, _counter_spell removing from game.stack._items + STACK zone → owner GRAVEYARD; can_cast/get_targets pattern), fdn_92 (Rite of Dragoncaller: `_is_on_battlefield`, register_triggers on SpellCastTriggeredEvent with self-guard, condition checks event.spell controller is source.controller and inst/sorc), fdn_192 (Burst Lightning any-target get_targets), fdn_205 (Wardens converge + tests).\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - Accidentally created duplicate tasks #14-#24 (dupes of #2-#12). Fixed by deleting #14-#24, keeping existing #2-#12.\n   - Write tool rejected on sos_4/card_impl.py with \"File has not been read yet\" — fixed by Read-ing the stub first, then Write succeeded. (Lesson: must Read each stub before Write.)\n   - No test failures encountered; all implemented cards passed on first run.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - Confirmed 1184-test baseline still passes with all 5 engine infrastructure edits.\n   - Designed casualty as \"stash spell in condition (only when returning True