{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   Implement 10 SOS (Strixhaven-themed) Magic: The Gathering card implementations in `/workspace/cards/sos/`, collector numbers: **1, 4, 13, 57, 97, 120, 201, 226, 245, 257**. Each card directory has `card_spec.json` (metadata) and `card_impl.py` (stub to fill with implementation class). User instructions:\n   - Use completed FDN cards in `/workspace/cards/fdn/` as implementation examples.\n   - Refer to `RULEBOOK.txt` (grep, don't read whole — ~961KB).\n   - Read engine source modules directly for API (rich docstrings).\n   - \"You are expected to make changes to the engine to implement new keywords and mechanics. The existing code base may not be perfect, you are free to make changes that don't break current behavior.\"\n\n   **CRITICAL CONSTRAINTS (must persist verbatim):**\n   - User: \"Do not modify any files under workspace/engine_tests/. These tests are staged for your local verification only; the runner uses its own authoritative copies for grading. Modifying the workspace tests will not change your score — it will only mislead you about whether your engine changes are correct.\"\n   - AGENTS.md Hard Rules: (1) Each card's implementation class must remain in `cards/sos/{card_id}/card_impl.py`; do not move/rename card directories. (2) Treat `engine_tests/` as read-only (no modify/add/delete); do NOT modify/delete existing FDN reference tests at `cards/fdn/fdn_*/tests.py` (may read, never edit); own SOS tests belong at `cards/sos/sos_<N>/tests.py`. (3) Additive-only engine modifications: MAY add new methods/classes/helpers/files inside `engine/` and MAY modify bodies of existing functions, but MUST NOT rename, move, or delete anything that already exists in `engine/` (no refactoring — breaks grader imports and zeros the score).\n   - Use `python3`.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - MTG engine (Python 3.11): zones, LIFO stack, triggers (APNAP), replacement effects, 7-layer continuous effects, SBAs, combat.\n   - Card hierarchy (engine/card.py): GameObject → CardImpl → Creature/Instant/Sorcery/Enchantment/Aura/Land/etc. CardImpl `_reset_characteristics()` resets ONLY `card_types` (to `_original_card_types`) and `keywords`. Creature `_reset_characteristics()` ALSO resets modified_power/toughness to base, plus_one/minus_one counters, combat-restriction flags (`_cant_attack`, `_cant_block`, `_cant_be_blocked`, `_cant_activate`, `_max_attackers_blocked`), protections. Creature defaults `summoning_sick=True`. Creature `power`/`toughness` are `@property` = `modified_power/toughness + plus_one_counters - minus_one_counters`.\n   - CardImpl hooks: can_cast, cost_reduction, on_cast, on_resolve, get_targets, register_triggers, register_replacement_effects, get_activated_abilities, get_modes. Land.can_cast→False; Land.get_mana_abilities→[]; Land `card_types` includes CardType.LAND; `is_tapped`.\n   - NEW additive hook (added in prior session): `static_cost_reduction(game, spell, spell_controller)->int`.\n   - Dataclasses (engine/card.py): `ManaAbility(cost, mana_produced, description)` where cost is `(game, source)->bool` (pays as side effect) and mana_produced is `(game)->None`. `ActivatedAbility(cost, effect, description)` where cost is `(game, source)->bool` and effect is `(game)->None`. `LoyaltyAbility(loyalty_cost, effect, description)`.\n   - Ability activation (engine/abilities.py): `activate_ability(game, player, ability)`. For non-mana abilities, `ability.cost(game, source)` is called; if True, effect is pushed as StackObject (resolved later). Mana abilities resolve effect immediately. `tap_cost(game, source)` helper. `ActivatedAbilityInstance(source, controller, cost, effect, is_mana_ability, description)`. No FDN tests invoke `activate_ability` directly — tests call cost/effect callables directly.\n   - Continuous effects (engine/continuous_effects.py): REAL `ContinuousEffect(source, layer, sublayer=None, apply=callable(game), timestamp=0, duration=DURATION_PERMANENT)`. Layer: COPY=1,CONTROL=2,TEXT=3,TYPE=4,COLOR=5,ABILITY=6,POWER_TOUGHNESS=7. SubLayer: CHARACTERISTIC_DEFINING=\"7a\", SET_PT=\"7b\", MODIFY_PT=\"7c\", COUNTERS=\"7d\". DURATION_PERMANENT=-1, DURATION_END_OF_TURN=0. `game.effect_manager.add(effect)`, `.remove_expired(game)`, `.apply_all(game)`. apply_all calls `_reset_objects` (calls `_reset_characteristics()` on each battlefield obj) then applies effects in layer/sublayer/timestamp order. **apply_all is ONLY auto-called at cleanup (turn.py:136).** The card.py `ContinuousEffect`/`Aura.apply_continuous_effect` is legacy.\n   - Keyword enum (engine/types.py) has ONLY evergreen keywords (FLYING, FIRST_STRIKE, DOUBLE_STRIKE, DEATHTOUCH, TRAMPLE, LIFELINK, VIGILANCE, REACH, HASTE, FLASH, DEFENDER, HEXPROOF, INDESTRUCTIBLE, MENACE, WARD, PROWESS). NO \"Prepared\"/Affinity/Casualty/Miracle/etc. Prowess has NO engine handler (just a flag). Only set real flags in `keywords`.\n   - ManaType: WHITE/BLUE/BLACK/RED/GREEN/COLORLESS. ManaCost.parse(\"{3}{R}{W}\"); ManaCost(generic=N); `.cmc`. mana_pool API: `.add(mana_type, n)`, `.total()`, `.can_pay(cost)->bool`, `.pay(cost)->bool`, `.empty()`, `last_payment_total`, `last_payment_colors`.\n   - Supertype: BASIC, LEGENDARY, SNOW.\n   - `engine.casting.cast_spell_free(game, player, card, from_zone)`: sets controller/owner, checks can_cast, moves card from from_zone→STACK, chooses targets via `card.get_targets(game)` (handles targeting internally), sets `card.mana_spent=0`, calls on_cast, pushes StackObject, fires SpellCastTriggeredEvent.\n   - `_resolve_spell(game, card, player, stack_obj)`: sets card.chosen_targets, calls on_resolve, then permanents→battlefield via move_to_zone, elif `getattr(card, \"_exile_instead_of_graveyard\", False)` → reset flag + move STACK→EXILE, else → graveyard. (The exile branch already exists and references The Dawning Archaic/Paradigm.)\n   - `engine.zones.move_to_zone(game, card, from_zone, to_zone, *, replacement_event=None)`: leaving battlefield uses controller's zone; otherwise owner's. Destination for graveyard/exile/hand/library is always owner. Registers triggers/replacement effects + fires EntersBattlefieldTriggeredEvent on entering battlefield; fires LeavesBattlefield/CreatureDies + unregisters on leaving.\n   - `engine.game` helpers: `deal_damage(game, source, target, amount)` (game.py:116; player target reduces life), `exile(game, obj)` (267), `draw_card(game, player)` (294; increments cards_drawn_this_turn BEFORE firing DrawsCardTriggeredEvent(player, card); returns card or None), `discard(game, player, card)` (338; move HAND→GRAVEYARD), `create_token(game, player, token)` (353; sets is_token/owner/controller, uses move_to_zone).\n   - Events (engine/events.py): AttacksTriggeredEvent(creature, attacker) [combat.py:269 fires `AttacksTriggeredEvent(creature=attacker, attacker=attacker)`]. SpellCastTriggeredEvent(spell, player, card, controller). DrawsCardTriggeredEvent(player, card). BeginningOfUpkeepTriggeredEvent() [NO fields; turn.py:204]. EntersBattlefieldTriggeredEvent(permanent, controller). BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent(phase, player).\n   - `TriggerRegistration(event_type, condition, effect, source, controller)`; condition `(game, event)->bool`, effect `(game)->None`. Pattern for stash: append to a per-card list ONLY when condition returns True; pop in effect (LIFO). `game.trigger_manager.register/unregister(source)`, `.fire_event(game, event)` (pushes StackObjects APNAP, does NOT resolve).\n   - Combat (engine/combat.py): `_can_attack(creature)` checks is_tapped, _cant_attack, DEFENDER, `getattr(creature, \"summoning_sick\", False)` + HASTE. declare_attackers_step eligibility = `[c for c in bf.get_all() if hasattr(c, \"base_power\") and _can_attack(c)]` (NO CardType.CREATURE check). `declare_attackers_step` calls `active.choose(eligible, ...)`, then fires AttacksTriggeredEvent per declared attacker.\n   - SBA (engine/state_based_actions.py): `_sba_creature_zero_toughness` = `if hasattr(obj, \"toughness\") and obj.toughness <= 0` (NO CardType.CREATURE check — DANGEROUS for lands exposing toughness). `_sba_creature_lethal_damage` requires `hasattr(obj,\"toughness\") and hasattr(obj,\"damage_marked\")`. `resolve_state_based_actions(game)`.\n   - `game.active_player` (property from active_player_index), `game.active_player_index`, `game.players[0/1]`. Untap step (turn.py:38-39) sets `summoning_sick=False` for any battlefield obj with the attribute.\n   - DeterministicPlayer: `_script` is a deque; `append()` adds right, `appendleft()` adds left, `popleft()` removes left. choose/choose_target/choose_yes_no/choose_card each pop ONE from left. `choose(options, desc)`, `choose_card(candidates, desc)`, `choose_yes_no(prompt)`. ScriptExhaustedError when empty.\n   - test_utils: `create_game()`, `set_board_state(game, idx, *, battlefield, hand, graveyard, life, mana)` (does NOT call register_triggers; sets owner/controller; does NOT set library), `cast_spell` (auto-resolves whole stack), `declare_attackers(game, [names])` (advances to combat, appendleft attackers, calls declare_attackers_step; does NOT priority_loop), `advance_to_phase`. `game.get_library/get_hand/get_graveyard/get_battlefield/get_exile(player)` return ZoneContainer with `.add/.remove/.get_all/.contains/.top(n)`.\n   - TESTING PATTERN: resolve manually `while not game.stack.is_empty(): game.stack.pop().on_resolve(game); resolve_state_based_actions(game)` (avoid priority_loop with scripted choices).\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_1/card_impl.py` (CREATED, all 7 tests pass):\n     ```python\n     class TheDawningArchaic(Creature):\n         def __init__(...): name=\"The Dawning Archaic\", mana_cost ManaCost.parse(\"{10}\"),\n             subtypes={\"Avatar\"}, supertypes={Supertype.LEGENDARY}, keywords=Keyword.REACH,\n             base_power=7, base_toughness=7\n         def cost_reduction(self, game): controller=self.controller; return 0 if None else len(_graveyard_castables(game, controller))\n         def register_triggers(self, game): TriggerRegistration on AttacksTriggeredEvent,\n             condition: _is_on_battlefield(g,source) and getattr(event,\"creature\",None) is source\n             effect: source._attack_cast(g)\n         def _attack_cast(self, game): candidates=_graveyard_castables(controller); if none return;\n             if not choose_yes_no(...) return; chosen=choose_card(candidates,...); if invalid return;\n             chosen._exile_instead_of_graveyard=True; cast_spell_free(game, controller, chosen, Zone.GRAVEYARD)\n     ```\n     Helpers: `_is_on_battlefield`, `_is_instant_or_sorcery`, `_graveyard_castables(game, player)`.\n   - `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_1/tests.py` (CREATED, 7 tests): `_DamageInstant` (deals 2 to opp, no targets), `_resolve_all`, `_isorc(n)`. Tests: properties (name/stats, keywords/types), cost reduction (counts inst+sorc not creature =2; clamped to generic 10 with 13 cards), attack cast (integration: set summoning_sick=False, phase=COMBAT/step=DECLARE_ATTACKERS, script=[True, zap], appendleft([archaic]), declare_attackers_step, _resolve_all → p2.life 18, zap in exile not graveyard), decline (script False, call _attack_cast directly), no-castable (only creature in gy → no choice consumed, stack empty).\n   - `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_257/card_impl.py` (CREATED, all 11 tests pass): `GreatHallOfTheBiblioplex(Land)`. Key design — P/T exposed only while animated:\n     ```python\n     def __init__: self._animated=False; self.modified_power=0; self.modified_toughness=0;\n         plus_one_counters=0; minus_one_counters=0; _base_plus_one_counters=0; _base_minus_one_counters=0;\n         damage_marked=0; summoning_sick=False; is_attacking=False; is_blocking=False; is_token=False;\n         dealt_deathtouch_damage=False\n     @property base_power: if not _animated: raise AttributeError; return 2\n     @property base_toughness: if not _animated: raise AttributeError; return 4\n     @property power: if not _animated: raise AttributeError; return modified_power+plus_one-minus_one\n     @property toughness: if not _animated: raise AttributeError; return modified_toughness+plus_one-minus_one\n     def _reset_characteristics: super()...; if _animated: card_types|={CREATURE}; subtypes|={\"Wizard\"};\n         modified_power=2; modified_toughness=4; counters=0; clear _cant_* flags, _max_attackers_blocked=1\n     def get_mana_abilities: [ManaAbility(_tap_only, _add_colorless, \"{T}: Add {C}.\"),\n         ManaAbility(_tap_pay_life, _add_any_color, \"{T}, Pay 1 life: ...\")]\n         _tap_pay_life checks life>=1, taps, life-=1. _add_any_color: controller.choose(W/U/B/R/G,...)\n     def get_activated_abilities: [ActivatedAbility(_cost, _effect, \"{5}: ...\")]\n         _cost: total()<5 return False; pay(ManaCost(generic=5)); return True. _effect: source._animate(game)\n     def _animate(self, game): if _animated return; _animated=True; card_types|={CREATURE};\n         subtypes|={\"Wizard\"}; modified_power=2; modified_toughness=4; damage_marked=0\n     def register_triggers: TriggerRegistration on SpellCastTriggeredEvent, condition requires\n         _animated + on battlefield + spell is controller's inst/sorc; effect source._pump(g)\n     def _pump(self, game): if not _animated return; modified_power+=1 (direct); register\n         ContinuousEffect(layer=POWER_TOUGHNESS, sublayer=MODIFY_PT, apply=(modified_power+=1), DURATION_END_OF_TURN)\n     ```\n   - `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_257/tests.py` (CREATED, 11 tests): `_resolve_all`, `_fire_cast(game, player, spell)`. Tests: is-land-not-creature (hasattr toughness/power False), can_cast False, colorless mana ability, any-color costs 1 life, animate to 2/4 Wizard still-land, insufficient mana, animate noop if already creature, pump per inst/sorc (3 then 4, toughness stays 4), no pump when not animated (stack empty), pump survives apply_all then expires after remove_expired+apply_all (3→3→2), un-animated land survives SBA.\n   - `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_201/card_impl.py` (CREATED, all 8 tests pass): `LoreholdTheHistorian(Creature)` {3}{R}{W} 5/5 {\"Elder\",\"Dragon\"} LEGENDARY FLYING|HASTE. `self._miracle_pending=[]`. register_triggers registers TWO triggers:\n     ```python\n     # Miracle on DrawsCardTriggeredEvent:\n     _miracle_condition: _is_on_battlefield + controller not None + event.player is controller +\n         event.card is inst/sorc + controller.cards_drawn_this_turn==1 → append card, return True\n     _miracle_effect: source._resolve_miracle(g)\n     def _resolve_miracle: pop pending card; if not in hand return; cost=ManaCost(generic=2);\n         if not can_pay return; if not choose_yes_no return; pay(cost); cast_spell_free(g, controller, card, Zone.HAND)\n     # Loot on BeginningOfUpkeepTriggeredEvent:\n     _loot_condition: _is_on_battlefield + ctrl not None + g.active_player is not ctrl\n     _loot_effect: source._resolve_loot(g)\n     def _resolve_loot: hand=list(...); if empty return; if not choose_yes_no return;\n         chosen=choose_card(hand,...); if invalid return; discard; draw_card\n     ```\n   - `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_201/tests.py` (CREATED, 8 tests): `_DamageInstant`(_4_R cost), `_resolve_all`, `_add_to_library(game, player, card)`. Tests: properties, miracle first instant castable for {2} (set cards_drawn_this_turn=0, draw_card, script [True] → p2.life 18, mana 0, in graveyard), decline miracle, no miracle for 2nd draw (cards_drawn=1 → stack empty), no miracle when Lorehold in hand not battlefield, loot opponent upkeep (active_player_index=1, script [True, junk] → junk in gy, fresh in hand), no loot on own upkeep (active_player_index=0 → stack empty).\n   - `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_13/card_spec.json` (READ): name \"Emeritus of Truce // Swords to Plowshares\", mana_cost \"{1}{W}{W} // {W}\", type_line \"Creature — Cat Cleric // Instant\", oracle_text \"When this creature enters, target player creates a 1/1 white and black Inkling creature token with flying. Then if an opponent controls more creatures than you, this creature becomes prepared. (While it's prepared, you may cast a copy of its spell. Doing so unprepares it.)\", power 3, toughness 3, colors [W], keywords [\"Prepared\"], complexity_tier \"complex\".\n   - `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_13/card_impl.py` (READ — still a stub with `class EmeritusOfTruceSwordsToPlowshares(CardImpl): pass`). NOT yet implemented.\n   - Reference files read this session: engine/card.py (ActivatedAbility/ManaAbility/ContinuousEffect dataclasses, Land, Creature, _reset_characteristics), engine/continuous_effects.py (full), engine/combat.py (_can_attack, declare_attackers_step), engine/state_based_actions.py (_sba_creature_zero_toughness/lethal), engine/casting.py (cast_spell_free, _resolve_spell exile branch, play_land), engine/abilities.py (activate_ability, ActivatedAbilityInstance, tap_cost), engine/turn.py (untap summoning_sick clear, upkeep/main event firing, cleanup apply_all), engine/game.py (draw_card, discard, exile/create_token/deal_damage line numbers), test_utils.py (full), cards/fdn/fdn_92 (Rite of Dragoncaller), fdn_267 (Secluded Courtyard), fdn_168 (Witness Protection), fdn_10 (EOT effect), fdn_106 (Loot — activated ability paying ManaCost(generic=6)), fdn_157 (Lightshell Duo prowess).\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - No test failures or errors occurred this session. All four implemented cards (SOS 1, 257, 201) passed pytest on first run (7, 11, 8 tests respectively).\n   - Resolved a critical DESIGN risk for SOS 257 before writing: discovered `_sba_creature_zero_toughness` has no CardType.CREATURE guard, so a Land exposing `toughness <= 0` would be destroyed. Solution: make `power`/`toughness`/`base_power`/`base_toughness` properties that RAISE AttributeError when `not self._animated`, so `hasattr` returns False and SBA/combat ignore the un-animated land.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - SOS 257 P/T-as-creature problem solved via AttributeError-raising properties + `_reset_characteristics` override re-establishing animation each apply_all cycle + dual (direct + registered EOT) pump for robustness whether or not apply_all is called mid-turn.\n   - SOS 201 miracle implemented via DrawsCardTriggeredEvent stash pattern (cards_drawn_this_turn==1 check verified correct since draw_card increments before firing) + pay {2} then cast_spell_free; loot via active_player comparison.\n   - Confirmed The Dawning Archaic's `_exile_instead_of_graveyard` infrastructure already exists in `_resolve_spell`.\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - (Session-opening, system reminders) Read tool results for sos_245/tests.py, sos_245/card_impl.py, sos_226/tests.py, sos_226/card_impl.py, sos_4/tests.py; deferred-tools list; prior continuation summary block.\n   - \"Tool loaded.\" (×2, after ToolSearch loaded task tools / TaskList/TaskUpdate)\n   - \"CRITICAL: Respond with TEXT ONLY. Do NOT call any tools... Your task is to create a detailed summary of the conversation so far...\" (final message requesting this summary)\n   - Security/constraint instructions preserved verbatim in section 1 (engine_tests/ read-only, FDN tests never edit, additive-only engine changes, card impl location).\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - #9 [in_progress] Implement SOS 13 Emeritus of Truce // Swords to Plowshares\n   - #10 Implement SOS 120 Improvisation Capstone\n   - #11 Implement SOS 97 Ral Zarek Guest Lecturer\n   - #12 Write SOS tests and run full pytest confirming no regressions (without touching engine_tests or FDN tests)\n   - Detailed designs ready (from prior summary):\n     - **Improvisation Capstone (Sorcery {5}{R}{R} Lesson)**: `_do_capstone` exiles top until total cmc>=4, choose_yes_no per castable → cast_spell_free from EXILE; on_resolve runs it + set _exile_instead_of_graveyard + register recurring BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent (event.player is ctrl, PRECOMBAT_MAIN) → choose_yes_no to repeat.\n     - **Ral Zarek (Planeswalker {1}{B}{B} starting_loyalty=3, Ral, LEGENDARY)**: get_loyalty_abilities=[+1 Surveil 2; -1 players discard; -2 return creature MV<=3 from GY; -7 flip 5 coins (allow `getattr(self,\"_forced_heads\",None)`) X=heads → `game.skip_turns[opp_index] += X`].\n\n8. Current Work:\n   Implementing SOS 13 Emeritus of Truce // Swords to Plowshares (task #9, in_progress). I had just confirmed via grep: `exile(game, obj)` exists (game.py:267), `create_token` (353), `deal_damage` (116), NO split-card infrastructure in engine, and \"Prepared\"/\"PREPARED\" is NOT in engine/types.py (so it is NOT a real keyword and must NOT be set in `keywords`). My planned design (not yet written):\n   - `class EmeritusOfTruceSwordsToPlowshares(Creature)`: name \"Emeritus of Truce // Swords to Plowshares\", mana_cost ManaCost.parse(\"{1}{W}{W}\"), subtypes {\"Cat\",\"Cleric\"}, base_power 3, base_toughness 3, NO legendary, NO keywords (Prepared isn't a real keyword). `self._prepared = False`.\n   - ETB implemented as a real trigger via `register_triggers` on EntersBattlefieldTriggeredEvent (condition: `getattr(event,\"permanent\",None) is source`) — NOT on_resolve — so the creature is already on the battlefield when counting (so it counts toward \"you\"). Effect `_etb`: `target_player = controller.choose(game.players, ...)`; create 1/1 Inkling flier token (subtypes {\"Inkling\"}, keywords Keyword.FLYING, is_token=True) via create_token for target_player; then if opponent's creature count > controller's creature count, set `self._prepared = True`.\n   - `get_activated_abilities`: returns the prepared STP ability only when `self._prepared` is True (or guard in cost). Cost: require `_prepared` + pay ManaCost.parse(\"{W}\") (cast a copy of its spell = pay {W}) + require a legal creature target exists. Effect `_cast_stp`: choose